 (docs last) | Docs describe default enablement for entitled clusters and the opt-out. |\n\nNo edge E001 → E004 / E005 / E006: the guardrails integration promotion, its\nvalidation, and the Dashboard default-on are fully specified by their HLRs\n(HLR-4, HLR-5) — the assessment inventories API stability, upgrade paths,\nscale limits, and error handling, which map to HLR-2/HLR-3 scope, and does not\nchange whether these epics exist or what they deliver. They start in parallel\nwith the assessment.\n\nNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics: Llama\nStack, TrustyAI, and the Dashboard are all existing platform components\n(architecture context files present, Konflux onboarded per context files), so\nRule 20 onboarding chains do not apply.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | The assessment itself is the epic deliverable. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 | API versioning, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases. |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | E003 | SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix — a distinct logical change (policy/matrix definition and validation) from E002 (API surface work), so two epics for the same component/team per the work-product boundary rule. |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | E004, E005 | One HLR covered by two epics across the component/team boundary: the distribution-side promotion (Llama Stack / RHOAI GenAI) and the service-side validation (TrustyAI / TrustyAI team). TrustyAI is otherwise passive in this strategy (Stable GA component; no other code changes), and the different-team validation triggers a separate validation epic rather than an AC on the nearest active component's epic. |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | E006 | Dashboard default enablement for entitled clusters. |\n| HLR-6 | P2 | E007 | Docs-authoring epic; priority P0 via the docs-authoring exception (strategy `priority: Critical`), not from HLR-6's P2 label — the P2 reads as relative value. |\n\nFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\nNo epic maps to HLRs at multiple priority levels, so no priority-split or\nbundling analysis is required. HLR-2 and HLR-3 are both P0 and are deliberately\nseparate epics (distinct deliverables and review cycles), not a priority split.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n  Non-Functional Requirements section. Teams were inferred from the\n  architecture context files (RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard) and ACs\n  were derived from the HLRs. Proceeding per Step 1's guidance.\n- **No Staff Engineer Input section** — no overrides to log.\n- **Docs priority inversion (managed)**: HLR-6 is P2 but the docs-authoring\n  epic is P0 by the deterministic exception rule (strategy priority Critical).\n  Reviewers should read E007's P0 as scheduling-neutral; per the rules it does\n  not propagate upstream.\n- **Scope sizing unknown (managed)**: E002/E003 scope is an estimate until the\n  assessment lands; both carry `gated_by` with `rewrite` semantics and fallback\n  approaches, and the assessment epic is first on the critical path so the\n  estimate resolves before the work starts.\n- **Component mapping note**: E007 uses canonical component `Documentation`\n  (present in `.context/rhai-components.txt`) for the docs-authoring epic; the\n  content concerns Llama Stack GA. There is no architecture-context file for\n  the `Documentation` component itself — expected for a docs-process label,\n  not a new-component signal (no onboarding chain generated).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable: there is no external dependency with uncertain timing. All\nwork is in-platform (midstream repos the teams control). The only uncertainty\nis internal (the GA scope assessment), handled as a gating Investigation\n(E001) rather than a tier split. E004/E005/E006 (P1) and E007 run as\nindependent parallel streams with the P0 assessment→stability/posture chain.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35111,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"951b2d0b-6a43-41e2-a296-3823ddb3c3f5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:48:48.509Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
