{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-01971e6b-c06b-4267-b4f2-757a3fa29f99","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa7a3115021e26ce","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-tzyru9i4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# API stability guarantees: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, TP upgrade path\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic puts a stability guarantee on Llama Stack's published API surface so\nenterprise customers can build production GenAI applications against it: the\nAPI surface becomes versioned, a deprecation policy is published and enforced,\nand a tested upgrade path exists from the last two Tech Preview releases. The\nspecific gaps to close are defined by the GA-readiness assessment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Version the published API surface of the Llama Stack distribution (the\n  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the LlamaStackDistribution-facing surfaces),\n  per the versioning approach the team selects.\n- Publish and enforce a deprecation policy for the versioned API surface:\n  how changes are announced, how long deprecated surfaces remain supported,\n  and how clients are expected to migrate.\n- Implement and test the upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases\n  to the GA release, including the distribution/operator upgrade mechanics.\n- Close the API-stability and error-handling gaps that the GA-readiness\n  assessment places in this workstream's scope (e.g., consistent error\n  responses on the versioned surface).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The published API surface carries explicit version identifiers, and the\n  versioning scheme is documented.\n- A deprecation policy is published, and any API change made in this epic\n  follows it (deprecated surfaces remain available for the policy's support\n  window).\n- The upgrade path from each of the last two Tech Preview releases is tested\n  and evidenced: a repeatable upgrade procedure exists and passes against a\n  representative distribution configuration, including data/CR migration where\n  applicable.\n- Clients written against the Tech Preview API surface continue to function\n  within the deprecation policy's compatibility window (no unannounced\n  breaking changes).\n- All API-stability and error-handling gaps assigned to this workstream by the\n  GA-readiness assessment are closed or explicitly deferred with rationale in\n  the assessment's tracking artifact.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n  two TP releases.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n  gated on that assessment, with re-scope expected rather than exceptional.\n  If the assessment finds the API surface already substantially meets the\n  bar, this epic narrows to deprecation-policy publication and upgrade-path\n  testing only.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38500,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"f81f8bfa-aaab-4c71-a906-299393a1c4b5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:12.123Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
