{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bbbd43b4-c4e4-4339-97b3-3e0483cf2473","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2ea923f435478e0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-tzyru9i4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E003.md","content":"# Production support posture: SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic establishes the production support posture required for Llama Stack\nGA: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a validated supported\nconfiguration matrix. It is the \"can Red Hat support this in production\"\nworkstream, distinct from the API surface work — different deliverables\n(policy documents and a validated matrix) and a different review cycle.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and document SLO targets for the GA Llama Stack distribution\n  (service-level objectives for the supported deployment model, as defined by\n  the team in line with platform support standards).\n- Define and document the backport policy: which release lines receive fixes\n  and for how long, aligned with the platform's support policy.\n- Define the supported configuration matrix: the distribution configurations\n  (deployment topologies, provider combinations, platform versions) that are\n  supported at GA.\n- Validate the matrix: run verification against each declared supported\n  configuration so the matrix ships as tested fact, not aspiration.\n- Fold in the scale-limit and error-handling gap outcomes from the GA\n  readiness assessment where they belong to support posture (documented\n  limits, support escalation paths).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented and published in the\n  support-posture artifact.\n- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines and\n  fix-backport rules.\n- The supported configuration matrix is published, and every configuration it\n  declares as supported has passed a verification run with recorded evidence.\n- No configuration is listed as supported without verification evidence; any\n  configuration that fails verification is listed as unsupported or removed,\n  with the failure recorded.\n- Support-posture gaps assigned to this workstream by the GA-readiness\n  assessment are closed or explicitly deferred with rationale.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- SLO targets and backport policy require product/support-organization\n  sign-off — budget review time from stakeholders outside the engineering\n  team.\n- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n  gated on that assessment. If the assessment finds existing platform support\n  standards already cover part of the posture, this epic narrows to\n  Llama-Stack-specific SLOs and matrix validation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39229,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"858f639e-c6bf-42c1-868e-c155826ca9c2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:21.631Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
