{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5ea408c1-ea16-4724-9a28-955321efce43","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e46e208099ea901","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-tzyru9i4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E004.md","content":"# Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack distributions\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes safety guardrails via TrustyAI a supported, documented\nintegration for GA Llama Stack distributions, instead of an experimental\nflag-gated option. Enterprise GA customers get guardrails as part of the\nsupported distribution, not as an opt-in experiment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration from the current experimental\n  flag-gated state to a supported integration in the GA Llama Stack\n  distribution, following the existing provider/safety-plugin wiring pattern.\n- Ensure the integration works with the distribution's supported deployment\n  model (TrustyAIService instances per project acting as the guardrails\n  provider for Llama Stack distributions).\n- Exercise the integration against the guardrails use cases the GA bar\n  requires (requests routed through the safety provider, policy outcomes\n  enforced) on a representative configuration.\n- Document the integration from the distribution side: what is supported,\n  how it is enabled and configured, and its supported state in the\n  configuration matrix.\n- Provide a disable/rollback path: the integration can be turned off via\n  distribution configuration without breaking the rest of the distribution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n  without any experimental/Tech Preview opt-in flag.\n- The integration is exercised end to end on a representative supported\n  configuration: requests subject to guardrails policies produce the expected\n  enforcement outcomes, with recorded evidence.\n- The integration is documented as supported, including enablement and\n  configuration guidance.\n- The integration can be disabled via configuration, and a distribution with\n  the integration disabled otherwise functions normally (rollback path).\n- Any GA-bar requirements the guardrails integration must meet for supported\n  status (error behavior, upgrade behavior) are verified and recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39943,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"9b3ce3c8-342a-4728-82c5-9ce5642f0dd6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:30.565Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
