ation scenarios\n  exercised jointly with the distribution-side integration, with\n  pass/fail results recorded.\n- Supported version combinations (TrustyAI service × Llama Stack\n  distribution) are documented, and each declared combination has validation\n  evidence.\n- Guardrails enforcement through the integration is verified: policies\n  configured on the TrustyAI service produce the expected outcomes for\n  requests routed from a Llama Stack distribution.\n- TrustyAI-side integration documentation exists, covering provisioning and\n  supported settings for the integration.\n- Any TrustyAI-side issues found during validation are either fixed or\n  recorded with disposition (supported workaround or documented limitation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions — the\n  TrustyAI-owned half of this requirement (service-side validation and\n  support of the integration).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40566,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"016a2d8a-3524-4990-993f-f7d8356d13f6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:40.040Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
