cs are reviewed and uplifted: no\n  Tech Preview caveats remain on GA-supported surfaces, and content matches\n  the shipped GA behavior.\n- A migration guide exists covering migration from the last two Tech Preview\n  releases, validated against the tested upgrade path (steps match what the\n  upgrade testing actually does).\n- The TrustyAI guardrails integration is documented as supported, consistent\n  with the validated integration behavior and supported version\n  combinations.\n- All published documentation is technically reviewed against the\n  implemented GA deliverables by the owning engineers, with review sign-off\n  recorded.\n- Documentation is published through the Red Hat docs content process for\n  the GA release.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-6 (P2)**: Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n  migration notes from TP.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41860,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6da8d12e10fd136","agent_id":"a14f6055297370552","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"06ffce3f-32a4-4eea-ab52-84b0f9afd360","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:49:58.407Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
