{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b6653ee4fb4778","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Production support posture: SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration\n4\t  matrix'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n6\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n7\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds existing platform support\n16\t    standards already cover the posture, this epic narrows to Llama-Stack-specific\n17\t    SLOs and matrix validation; the definitive GA scope list from the assessment governs\n18\t    the final contents.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Production support posture: SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic establishes the production support posture required for Llama Stack\n41\tGA: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a validated supported\n42\tconfiguration matrix. It is the \"can Red Hat support this in production\"\n43\tworkstream, distinct from the API surface work — different deliverables\n44\t(policy documents and a validated matrix) and a different review cycle.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Define and document SLO targets for the GA Llama Stack distribution\n49\t  (service-level objectives for the supported deployment model, as defined by\n50\t  the team in line with platform support standards).\n51\t- Define and document the backport policy: which release lines receive fixes\n52\t  and for how long, aligned with the platform's support policy.\n53\t- Define the supported configuration matrix: the distribution configurations\n54\t  (deployment topologies, provider combinations, platform versions) that are\n55\t  supported at GA.\n56\t- Validate the matrix: run verification against each declared supported\n57\t  configuration so the matrix ships as tested fact, not aspiration.\n58\t- Fold in the scale-limit and error-handling gap outcomes from the GA\n59\t  readiness assessment where they belong to support posture (documented\n60\t  limits, support escalation paths).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented and published in the\n65\t  support-posture artifact.\n66\t- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines and\n67\t  fix-backport rules.\n68\t- The supported configuration matrix is published, and every configuration it\n69\t  declares as supported has passed a verification run with recorded evidence.\n70\t- No configuration is listed as supported without verification evidence; any\n71\t  configuration that fails verification is listed as unsupported or removed,\n72\t  with the failure recorded.\n73\t- Support-posture gaps assigned to this workstream by the GA-readiness\n74\t  assessment are closed or explicitly deferred with rationale.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n79\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n80\t\n81\t## Risks / Notes\n82\t\n83\t- SLO targets and backport policy require product/support-organization\n84\t  sign-off — budget review time from stakeholders outside the engineering\n85\t  team.\n86\t- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n87\t  gated on that assessment. If the assessment finds existing platform support\n88\t  standards already cover part of the posture, this epic narrows to\n89\t  Llama-Stack-specific SLOs and matrix validation.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbef671f2f1c4d7e","agent_id":"a949b8667dcb016b9","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"d93b7bf8-9c61-47af-8e69-ae98be1136a6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:52:13.606Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80b6653ee4fb4778","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
