guration.\n50\t- Document the integration from the distribution side: what is supported,\n51\t  how it is enabled and configured, and its supported state in the\n52\t  configuration matrix.\n53\t- Provide a disable/rollback path: the integration can be turned off via\n54\t  distribution configuration without breaking the rest of the distribution.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n59\t  without any experimental/Tech Preview opt-in flag.\n60\t- The integration is exercised end to end on a representative supported\n61\t  configuration: requests subject to guardrails policies produce the expected\n62\t  enforcement outcomes, with recorded evidence.\n63\t- The integration is documented as supported, including enablement and\n64\t  configuration guidance.\n65\t- The integration can be disabled via configuration, and a distribution with\n66\t  the integration disabled otherwise functions normally (rollback path).\n67\t- Any GA-bar requirements the guardrails integration must meet for supported\n68\t  status (error behavior, upgrade behavior) are verified and recorded.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n73\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbef671f2f1c4d7e","agent_id":"a949b8667dcb016b9","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"47dcd19a-7e7e-4095-babe-26acb4b7c747","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:52:14.172Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-822ad434647bbd5c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
