inations.\n50\t- Record validation evidence: guardrails policies enforced through the\n51\t  integration, service behavior under distribution load and error conditions\n52\t  relevant to the GA bar.\n53\t- Make any TrustyAI-side adjustments required for the integration to be\n54\t  supported (service behavior, documentation of the integration contract from\n55\t  the TrustyAI side), if validation surfaces them.\n56\t- Document TrustyAI-side integration requirements (provisioning, sizing,\n57\t  supported TrustyAIService settings) for customers using the integration.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A validation report exists covering the guardrails integration scenarios\n62\t  exercised jointly with the distribution-side integration, with\n63\t  pass/fail results recorded.\n64\t- Supported version combinations (TrustyAI service × Llama Stack\n65\t  distribution) are documented, and each declared combination has validation\n66\t  evidence.\n67\t- Guardrails enforcement through the integration is verified: policies\n68\t  configured on the TrustyAI service produce the expected outcomes for\n69\t  requests routed from a Llama Stack distribution.\n70\t- TrustyAI-side integration documentation exists, covering provisioning and\n71\t  supported settings for the integration.\n72\t- Any TrustyAI-side issues found during validation are either fixed or\n73\t  recorded with disposition (supported workaround or documented limitation).\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n78\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions — the\n79\t  TrustyAI-owned half of this requirement (service-side validation and\n80\t  support of the integration).\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbef671f2f1c4d7e","agent_id":"a949b8667dcb016b9","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"0e8a803f-88aa-4c60-8129-e0372216c65d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:52:17.619Z","to