{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81f92cc479d5ba57","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack\n4\t  distributions\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n6\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n7\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack distributions\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes safety guardrails via TrustyAI a supported, documented\n35\tintegration for GA Llama Stack distributions, instead of an experimental\n36\tflag-gated option. Enterprise GA customers get guardrails as part of the\n37\tsupported distribution, not as an opt-in experiment.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration from the current experimental\n42\t  flag-gated state to a supported integration in the GA Llama Stack\n43\t  distribution, following the existing provider/safety-plugin wiring pattern.\n44\t- Ensure the integration works with the distribution's supported deployment\n45\t  model (TrustyAIService instances per project acting as the guardrails\n46\t  provider for Llama Stack distributions).\n47\t- Exercise the integration against the guardrails use cases the GA bar\n48\t  requires (requests routed through the safety provider, policy outcomes\n49\t  enforced) on a representative configuration.\n50\t- Document the integration from the distribution side: what is supported,\n51\t  how it is enabled and configured, and its supported state in the\n52\t  configuration matrix.\n53\t- Provide a disable/rollback path: the integration can be turned off via\n54\t  distribution configuration without breaking the rest of the distribution.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n59\t  without any experimental/Tech Preview opt-in flag.\n60\t- The integration is exercised end to end on a representative supported\n61\t  configuration: requests subject to guardrails policies produce the expected\n62\t  enforcement outcomes, with recorded evidence.\n63\t- The integration is documented as supported, including enablement and\n64\t  configuration guidance.\n65\t- The integration can be disabled via configuration, and a distribution with\n66\t  the integration disabled otherwise functions normally (rollback path).\n67\t- Any GA-bar requirements the guardrails integration must meet for supported\n68\t  status (error behavior, upgrade behavior) are verified and recorded.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n73\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fccc655639e079","agent_id":"a6f5ddbc43ece28a3","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"d4baf65f-9716-4afe-ab5c-2be84b2271be","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:55:24.419Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81f92cc479d5ba57","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
