the versioning approach the team selects.\n50\t- Publish and enforce a deprecation policy for the versioned API surface:\n51\t  how changes are announced, how long deprecated surfaces remain supported,\n52\t  and how clients are expected to migrate.\n53\t- Implement and test the upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases\n54\t  to the GA release, including the distribution/operator upgrade mechanics.\n55\t- Close the API-stability and error-handling gaps that the GA-readiness\n56\t  assessment places in this workstream's scope (e.g., consistent error\n57\t  responses on the versioned surface).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- The published API surface carries explicit version identifiers, and the\n62\t  versioning scheme is documented.\n63\t- A deprecation policy is published, and any API change made in this epic\n64\t  follows it (deprecated surfaces remain available for the policy's support\n65\t  window).\n66\t- The upgrade path from each of the last two Tech Preview releases is tested\n67\t  and evidenced: a repeatable upgrade procedure exists and passes against a\n68\t  representative distribution configuration, including data/CR migration where\n69\t  applicable.\n70\t- Clients written against the Tech Preview API surface continue to function\n71\t  within the deprecation policy's compatibility window (no unannounced\n72\t  breaking changes).\n73\t- All API-stability and error-handling gaps assigned to this workstream by the\n74\t  GA-readiness assessment are closed or explicitly deferred with rationale in\n75\t  the assessment's tracking artifact.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n80\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n81\t  two TP releases.\n82\t\n83\t## Risks / Notes\n84\t\n85\t- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n86\t  gated on that assessment, with re-scope expected rather than exceptional.\n87\t  If the assessment finds the API surface already substantially meets the\n88\t  bar, this epic narrows to deprecation-policy publication and upgrade-path\n89\t  testing only.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fccc655639e079","agent_id":"a6f5ddbc43ece28a3","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"069f1a5c-a4f4-4186-a7da-5a6da735a3bf","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:58:08.367Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a797100197c157c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
