{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5c744e28d0a63da","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E006\n3\ttitle: Enable Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThe Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled\n34\tclusters: the Tech Preview opt-in gate is removed so that entitled customers\n35\tsee Llama Stack management without any enablement step. This is the\n36\tDashboard's contribution to Llama Stack GA — the management UI moves from\n37\topt-in experiment to default-on for entitled users.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Remove the Tech Preview opt-in gate for Llama Stack management in the\n42\t  Dashboard: Llama Stack management surfaces (navigation, resource views, and\n43\t  management flows) are enabled by default for entitled clusters.\n44\t- Preserve entitlement-based gating: enablement follows cluster entitlement,\n45\t  replacing the manual opt-in.\n46\t- Keep a supported opt-out: administrators can disable Llama Stack management\n47\t  via the Dashboard's existing configuration mechanism (feature\n48\t  flags/defaults in the OdhDashboardConfig CR), so the default flip is\n49\t  reversible without a code change.\n50\t- Update Dashboard-side messaging/status so Llama Stack management no longer\n51\t  presents as Tech Preview (labels, flags referencing preview status that\n52\t  fall out of this change).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- On an entitled cluster with no explicit configuration, Llama Stack\n57\t  management is available in the Dashboard without any opt-in step.\n58\t- On a non-entitled cluster, Llama Stack management is not enabled by this\n59\t  change (existing entitlement behavior is preserved).\n60\t- An administrator can disable Llama Stack management through supported\n61\t  configuration, verified by test (rollback/opt-out path).\n62\t- No Tech Preview opt-in gate remains in the Llama Stack management flow.\n63\t- Existing user preferences/configurations set during the Tech Preview period\n64\t  are respected (an explicit opt-in or opt-out made previously is not\n65\t  silently overridden).\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-5 (P1)**: The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n70\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fccc655639e079","agent_id":"a6f5ddbc43ece28a3","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"cca5e3d0-bf46-4fa6-84fe-483e173eaf08","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:58:09.626Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5c744e28d0a63da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
