{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-80917ef1753e656b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability (RHAISTRAT-9014)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: neither below-threshold nor docs-only. The strategy spans three\n13\tcomponents (Llama Stack, TrustyAI, Dashboard) owned by three teams, carries\n14\tP0/P1/P2 HLRs, and contains a genuine unknown (the GA scope itself is not yet\n15\tinventoried — the strategy's open question states the size of the stability\n16\tand hardening work is an estimate until HLR-1's assessment lands). Full\n17\tmulti-epic decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n22\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 | GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 | API stability guarantees: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, TP upgrade path | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 | Production support posture: SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 | Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack distributions | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 | TrustyAI-side validation of the guardrails integration for GA distributions | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 | Enable Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E007 | GA documentation uplift with TP migration notes | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n30\t\n31\tPriorities: E001 is P0 because it transitively enables all P0 GA work\n32\t(HLR-2, HLR-3). E004 is P0 by priority inheritance, not from HLR-4's P1\n33\tlabel: the supported configuration matrix (P0, HLR-3) must include the\n34\tTrustyAI guardrails configuration as supported at GA, so the promotion\n35\ttransitively enables P0 work (see the E004 → E003 edge). E005 remains P1 —\n36\tit blocks only the docs epic, whose P0 does not propagate (docs-authoring\n37\texception). E007's P0 derives from the docs-authoring priority exception\n38\t(strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), not from inheritance — it\n39\tdoes not push priority upstream.\n40\t\n41\t## Dependency DAG\n42\t\n43\t```mermaid\n44\tgraph TD\n45\t  E001[\"E001 GA-readiness assessment (Inv)\"] --> E002[\"E002 API stability\"]\n46\t  E001 --> E003[\"E003 Support posture\"]\n47\t  E004[\"E004 TrustyAI integration (distro)\"] --> E005[\"E005 TrustyAI validation\"]\n48\t  E004 --> E003\n49\t  E002 --> E007[\"E007 GA docs\"]\n50\t  E003 --> E007\n51\t  E004 --> E007\n52\t  E005 --> E007\n53\t  E006[\"E006 Dashboard default-on\"] --> E007\n54\t```\n55\t\n56\t## DAG Justification\n57\t\n58\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n59\t|------|------|-----------|\n60\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The GA-readiness assessment produces the definitive GA scope; the size and content of the API stability and hardening work is explicitly an estimate until it lands (strategy open question). True gate: `rewrite` — the assessment outcome can change what the stability work includes. |\n61\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | Same assessment defines the GA bar for support posture (which configurations must be supported, what the error-handling/scale gaps are). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n62\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 12 (artifact producer → consumer) | The TrustyAI team's validation epic verifies the integration wired into the GA distribution; the validation deliverable builds against the integration artifact, so it is serial. |\n63\t| E002 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Migration notes and GA docs describe the versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and tested upgrade path once built. |\n64\t| E003 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | GA documentation must reflect the published SLO targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. |\n65\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Docs cover the TrustyAI guardrails integration as supported. |\n66\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Docs reflect the TrustyAI-side supported-integration validation outcomes. |\n67\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Docs describe default enablement for entitled clusters and the opt-out. |\n68\t\n69\tNo edge E001 → E004 / E005 / E006: the guardrails integration promotion, its\n70\tvalidation, and the Dashboard default-on are fully specified by their HLRs\n71\t(HLR-4, HLR-5) — the assessment inventories API stability, upgrade paths,\n72\tscale limits, and error handling, which map to HLR-2/HLR-3 scope, and does not\n73\tchange whether these epics exist or what they deliver. They start in parallel\n74\twith the assessment.\n75\t\n76\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics: Llama\n77\tStack, TrustyAI, and the Dashboard are all existing platform components\n78\t(architecture context files present, Konflux onboarded per context files), so\n79\tRule 20 onboarding chains do not apply.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n82\t\n83\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n84\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n85\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | The assessment itself is the epic deliverable. |\n86\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 | API versioning, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases. |\n87\t| HLR-3 | P0 | E003 | SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix — a distinct logical change (policy/matrix definition and validation) from E002 (API surface work), so two epics for the same component/team per the work-product boundary rule. |\n88\t| HLR-4 | P1 | E004, E005 | One HLR covered by two epics across the component/team boundary: the distribution-side promotion (Llama Stack / RHOAI GenAI) and the service-side validation (TrustyAI / TrustyAI team). TrustyAI is otherwise passive in this strategy (Stable GA component; no other code changes), and the different-team validation triggers a separate validation epic rather than an AC on the nearest active component's epic. |\n89\t| HLR-5 | P1 | E006 | Dashboard default enablement for entitled clusters. |\n90\t| HLR-6 | P2 | E007 | Docs-authoring epic; priority P0 via the docs-authoring exception (strategy `priority: Critical`), not from HLR-6's P2 label — the P2 reads as relative value. |\n91\t\n92\tFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\n93\tNo epic maps to HLRs at multiple priority levels, so no priority-split or\n94\tbundling analysis is required. HLR-2 and HLR-3 are both P0 and are deliberately\n95\tseparate epics (distinct deliverables and review cycles), not a priority split.\n96\t\n97\t## Health Warnings\n98\t\n99\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n100\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n101\t  Non-Functional Requirements section. Teams were inferred from the\n102\t  architecture context files (RHOAI GenAI, TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard) and ACs\n103\t  were derived from the HLRs. Proceeding per Step 1's guidance.\n104\t- **No Staff Engineer Input section** — no overrides to log.\n105\t- **Docs priority inversion (managed)**: HLR-6 is P2 but the docs-authoring\n106\t  epic is P0 by the deterministic exception rule (strategy priority Critical).\n107\t  Reviewers should read E007's P0 as scheduling-neutral; per the rules it does\n108\t  not propagate upstream.\n109\t- **Scope sizing unknown (managed)**: E002/E003 scope is an estimate until the\n110\t  assessment lands; both carry `gated_by` with `rewrite` semantics and fallback\n111\t  approaches, and the assessment epic is first on the critical path so the\n112\t  estimate resolves before the work starts.\n113\t- **Component mapping note**: E007 uses canonical component `Documentation`\n114\t  (present in `.context/rhai-components.txt`) for the docs-authoring epic; the\n115\t  content concerns Llama Stack GA. There is no architecture-context file for\n116\t  the `Documentation` component itself — expected for a docs-process label,\n117\t  not a new-component signal (no onboarding chain generated).\n118\t\n119\t## Tiered Delivery\n120\t\n121\tNot applicable: there is no external dependency with uncertain timing. All\n122\twork is in-platform (midstream repos the teams control). The only uncertainty\n123\tis internal (the GA scope assessment), handled as a gating Investigation\n124\t(E001) rather than a tier split. E004/E005/E006 (P1) and E007 run as\n125\tindependent parallel streams with the P0 assessment→stability/posture chain.\n126\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b03c5b8988ba3b1","agent_id":"a19fbb2abe9512236","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"f99e2980-e052-48ab-9e9f-5e287adf66d8","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:59:40.884Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-80917ef1753e656b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
