n51\t  the team in line with platform support standards).\n52\t- Define and document the backport policy: which release lines receive fixes\n53\t  and for how long, aligned with the platform's support policy.\n54\t- Define the supported configuration matrix: the distribution configurations\n55\t  (deployment topologies, provider combinations, platform versions) that are\n56\t  supported at GA.\n57\t- Validate the matrix: run verification against each declared supported\n58\t  configuration so the matrix ships as tested fact, not aspiration.\n59\t- Include the TrustyAI guardrails integration configuration in the matrix\n60\t  once it is promoted to supported status in the GA distribution: the\n61\t  promotion and its end-to-end evidence land in the distribution-side\n62\t  guardrails work this epic is sequenced after, and this epic verifies the\n63\t  configuration and records the evidence in the matrix entry.\n64\t- Fold in the scale-limit and error-handling gap outcomes from the GA\n65\t  readiness assessment where they belong to support posture (documented\n66\t  limits, support escalation paths).\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented and published in the\n71\t  support-posture artifact.\n72\t- The backport policy is documented, covering supported release lines and\n73\t  fix-backport rules.\n74\t- The supported configuration matrix is published, and every configuration it\n75\t  declares as supported has passed a verification run with recorded evidence.\n76\t- No configuration is listed as supported without verification evidence; any\n77\t  configuration that fails verification is listed as unsupported or removed,\n78\t  with the failure recorded.\n79\t- The TrustyAI guardrails integration configuration is included in the\n80\t  published matrix as supported, with verification evidence recorded from a\n81\t  run against the promoted integration.\n82\t- Support-posture gaps assigned to this workstream by the GA-readiness\n83\t  assessment are closed or explicitly deferred with rationale.\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n88\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix.\n89\t\n90\t## Risks / Notes\n91\t\n92\t- SLO targets and backport policy require product/support-organization\n93\t  sign-off — budget review time from stakeholders outside the engineering\n94\t  team.\n95\t- Scope is an estimate until the GA-readiness assessment lands; this epic is\n96\t  gated on that assessment. If the assessment finds existing platform support\n97\t  standards already cover part of the posture, this epic narrows to\n98\t  Llama-Stack-specific SLOs and matrix validation.\n99\t- Re-split trigger: if the assessment places more support-posture scope in\n100\t  this workstream than one sprint of estimated effort (beyond SLO/backport\n101\t  policy definition and matrix validation), re-split along the assessment's\n102\t  gap categories (policy definition vs. matrix validation runs) so no epic\n103\t  exceeds the ~2-week guideline.\n104\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b03c5b8988ba3b1","agent_id":"a19fbb2abe9512236","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"be96f416-4e58-4b7a-ad77-27a0cbdc0c68","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:59:47.505Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f3e16dbe9c2e5fe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
