{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e331f2406b1a191","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack\n4\t  distributions\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n6\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n7\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Promote TrustyAI guardrails integration to supported status in Llama Stack distributions\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic makes safety guardrails via TrustyAI a supported, documented\n35\tintegration for GA Llama Stack distributions, instead of an experimental\n36\tflag-gated option. Enterprise GA customers get guardrails as part of the\n37\tsupported distribution, not as an opt-in experiment.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration from the current experimental\n42\t  flag-gated state to a supported integration in the GA Llama Stack\n43\t  distribution, following the existing provider/safety-plugin wiring pattern.\n44\t- Ensure the integration works with the distribution's supported deployment\n45\t  model (TrustyAIService instances per project acting as the guardrails\n46\t  provider for Llama Stack distributions).\n47\t- Exercise the integration against the guardrails use cases the GA bar\n48\t  requires (requests routed through the safety provider, policy outcomes\n49\t  enforced) on a representative configuration.\n50\t- Document the integration from the distribution side: what is supported,\n51\t  how it is enabled and configured, and its supported state as an entry in\n52\t  the supported configuration matrix, together with the end-to-end\n53\t  verification evidence that entry requires. The matrix itself is published\n54\t  and verified in the support-posture workstream, which is sequenced after\n55\t  this epic so the guardrails entry and its evidence are in place before the\n56\t  matrix ships. (This documentation is the engineering-source reference for\n57\t  the integration; user-facing documentation is authored separately through\n58\t  the Red Hat docs content process.)\n59\t- Provide a disable/rollback path: the integration can be turned off via\n60\t  distribution configuration without breaking the rest of the distribution.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A Llama Stack distribution can be configured with TrustyAI guardrails\n65\t  without any experimental/Tech Preview opt-in flag.\n66\t- The integration is exercised end to end on a representative supported\n67\t  configuration: requests subject to guardrails policies produce the expected\n68\t  enforcement outcomes, with recorded evidence.\n69\t- The integration is documented as supported, including enablement and\n70\t  configuration guidance.\n71\t- The integration's supported state is declared for the supported\n72\t  configuration matrix with the recorded end-to-end evidence, so the\n73\t  support-posture matrix entry for the guardrails configuration can be\n74\t  published and verified from this epic's deliverables.\n75\t- The integration can be disabled via configuration, and a distribution with\n76\t  the integration disabled otherwise functions normally (rollback path).\n77\t- Any GA-bar requirements the guardrails integration must meet for supported\n78\t  status (error behavior, upgrade behavior) are verified and recorded.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n83\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b03c5b8988ba3b1","agent_id":"a19fbb2abe9512236","session_id":"e26389fa-88dc-429a-9f52-aa484b1f6aa7","uuid":"8f9c9525-a8cf-4c32-96d6-bb9136a2a44a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:59:48.125Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e331f2406b1a191","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
